From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:31:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(a2ui): render CheckBox as CLIO's own checkbox with a
 real hit target

The kernel catalog took CheckBox straight from the upstream basic catalog, so
an agent's checkboxes were bare 13 px native boxes with bold labels against
them (live 2026-11-18: an EarthScope station picker). Every other interactive
control already had a CLIO wrapper. ClioCheckBox uses the shared Radix
checkbox; the whole row (box and label) is the hit target, at least 36 px tall
and 44 px on touch, and a failed check is shown in words beside the box.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
